    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0024" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859A.20/213: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister to the Norwegian Government in Exile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-26T20:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian Series No. 15. Your 17.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d24-f1"/> War Department
                    approves draft exchange of notes as telegraphed in your no. 16 and recommends
                    that agreement be consummated as soon as possible. Accordingly, you are
                    authorized to proceed with exchange of notes<anchor n="19" xml:id="d24-f2"/>
                    “acting under instructions of your Government”.</p>
                <p>Texts of notes as signed should be sent to Department by air mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d24-f1" n="18" xml:id="d24-f1-content">
                <p>Dated August 13, 11 p.m.; not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d24-f2" n="19" xml:id="d24-f2-content">
                <p>The notes exchanged between Minister Biddle and Mr. Lie, the Norwegian Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs, on August 28 were the same as draft quoted in Norwegian
                    Series telegram No. 16, July 9, 7 p.m., <ref target="#pg12">p. 12</ref>. For
                    final text of notes, see Department of State Executive Agreement Series No. 497,
                    or 59 Stat. (pt. 2) 1819.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
